   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Francesco,<div><br></div><div>Thank you very much for the swift reply.</div><div>Brilliant! Will try that option then.</div><div><br></div><div>J</div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Tuesday, July 24, 2018 at 11:57:27 AM UTC+1, Francesco Favero wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi Joao,<div><br></div><div>yes, you can define breakpoints in the extract step (bypassing the built-in segmentation).</div><div>You need a data.frame file with 3 columns: chrom, start.pos end.pos.</div><div>Then, when you run sequenza.extract you use the object with the breaks option:</div><div><br></div><div>    my_breaks &lt;- read.table(“my_curated_bed_file.txt”, header=F, sep=“\\t”, stringsAsFactor=FALSE)</div><div>    colnames(my_breaks) &lt;- c(“chrom”, “start.pos”, “end.pos&quot;)</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div>    test &lt;- sequenza.extract(my_seqz_file, breaks=my_breaks)<br><div><br></div><div>Unfortunately there isn’t a easy way to automatically provide the “right” segmentation for the 2 samples, I usually end up doing a visual inspection with chromosome.view and manually curate the breaks in the segments file</div><div><br></div><div>There are multi-sample segmentation options, but not with the allele frequency taken into account.</div><div><br></div><div>Francesco</div><div> </div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 24 Jul 2018, at 11.37, Joao Miguel Alves &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">jmfernan...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
